        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(proxy-capture): honor response backpressure and client abort",
        "body": "Closes #105701\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the debug proxy capture server would forward upstream response bodies without honoring `ServerResponse.write()` backpressure, and could crash or leave work running when a client aborted mid-stream. Operators and test fixtures using the debug proxy could see unbounded memory growth under slow clients and unhandled write errors on disconnect.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe HTTP response forward path uses Node native `Readable.pipe()` for backpressure, keeps body-preview capture as an independent `data` observer, cancels upstream on client abort, and preserves pre-header 502 / post-header abort behavior on upstream errors. Existing partial-upstream-error behavior (complete 502 before headers / abort after headers) is preserved.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDebug proxy traffic capture remains available for local diagnostics and fixture recording, but slow clients no longer force unbounded buffering of upstream response data, and mid-response client aborts no longer leave the proxy in a fragile write-after-end state. No product config or user-facing channel behavior changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Verification host:** local macOS (agent; CS option 1 follow-up)\n\nCommands run after native-pipe refactor:\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check src/proxy-capture/proxy-server.ts src/proxy-capture/proxy-server.test.ts\n# pass\n\npnpm exec oxlint src/proxy-capture/proxy-server.ts src/proxy-capture/proxy-server.test.ts\n# 0 warnings / 0 errors\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/proxy-capture/proxy-server.test.ts\n# 9/9 passed\n\n# Real proxy process proof (origin + startDebugProxyServer in-process listeners,\n# real HTTP clients over loopback — not unit Fake streams):\n# slow client pause-after-first-chunk, mid-response abort, subsequent /healthy\n```\n\nFocused tests:\n- native pipe backpressure + capture observer\n- client abort destroys upstream\n- mid-response abort + later healthy request through same proxy\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior addressed: Debug proxy forwards upstream bodies via Node native `Readable.pipe()` backpressure; preview capture is an independent `data` observer; client abort cancels upstream; later requests still succeed.\n- Environment: local macOS, branch tip after CS follow-up commit, Node via `pnpm exec tsx` / `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs`.\n- Current-main contrast: main ignored `write()` false (no backpressure). First PR revision used a hand-written pause/drain controller; CS asked for native pipe + real-process proof.\n- Exact steps after this patch:\n  1. Refactor `pipeUpstreamBodyToClient` to `upstreamRes.pipe(res)` with capture observer + abort cancel.\n  2. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/proxy-capture/proxy-server.test.ts` → 9/9.\n  3. Real-process proof: start streaming origin + `startDebugProxyServer` listeners; HTTP client slow-read; abort after first chunk; GET `/healthy` on same proxy.\n- Evidence after fix (redacted loopback ports):\n\n```text\n[proof] origin listening on 127.0.0.1:65525\n[proof] proxy process server listening on http://127.0.0.1:65526\n[proof] step1: slow client through real proxy\n[proof] slow client: pausing reads for 200ms after first chunk\n[proof] step1 done: status=200 chunks=202 bodyBytes=1905 aborted=false\n[proof] step2: mid-response client abort\n[proof] client abort after first chunk (8 bytes)\n[proof] step2 done: aborted=true chunks=1\n[proof] step3: subsequent healthy request on same proxy\n[proof] step3 done: status=200 body=\"ok\" complete=true\n[proof] PASS: real proxy survived slow client + abort and served later request\n```\n\n- Control check: unit suite still covers capture + abort destroy; vitest 9/9 green; oxlint/oxfmt clean on touched files.\n- Observed result: slow client completed; abort cancelled mid-stream; subsequent healthy returned 200 `ok` on the same proxy.\n- What was not tested: CONNECT tunnel backpressure (still socket pipe), multi-GB responses, non-macOS hosts, full-repo CI.\n\n## AI disclosure\n\nThis fix was authored with AI assistance (Grok). Human operator owns the contributor fork push and PR submission policy for this pipeline.\n\n",
